I think another such level or two will do the trick.  Giant
corpses seem to give a pretty good boost.

In the meantime, I unintentionally ran into Master Kaen---while
fainting, no less---and got the best of him.  I'd gone on the
quest without the intention of going to the end, just to see
what I could pick up, and I fell through a trap door and ended
up about two squares away from him.  I hit him with a spell of
sleep, and wacked him twice with Excalibur.  He then woke up,
cursed one of the odd wands in my inventory, and teleported off
to the right.  Somewhere in there, I'd gotten a message about
being weak, and thought it was something he'd done.  I started
wading through the X's and the H's, trying to get to where he'd
gone, when I fainted.  At least all of the X's and H's would
stop him from getting near me.  When I finally got some food out
of my bag and ate it, I couldn't find him any more.  All things
considered, however, I thought it best to get out of there, and
come back when I was more prepared.  So I zapped a wand of
teleport to get to the stairs, and went up.  And there he was,
two squares away.  I figured I'd get in one ranged attack (spell
of fireball), and then go back down---there may have been a lot
of X's and H's, but they didn't seem to be doing much damage.
But much to my surprise, that one attack finished him off.

All in all, he didn't seem as bad as he's made out to be.  But I
can't say that I'd recommend doing it the way I just did as a
general rule: had I fainted a move or two earlier, before he
teleported away, I think I'd have been done for.  Even worse:
had his curse hit my bag of holding, instead of some random
wand, I might not have been able to get the food from it.  I can
just see it now: kill Master Kaen, and die of hunger on the next
move.

Anyway, next on schedule is Juiblex' swamp.  I'm still on the
look-out for some more scrolls of gold detection, some more
wands of death (only one seems a bit few for a final run), and
to improve my AC.  But all in all, it's going very good.

